codex
RED is reproduced cleanly: both 12-way cases fail at the nested checkout with `timeout exceeded when trying to connect`—same-run and twelve distinct runs. I’m switching to non-blocking `pg_try_advisory_lock`, threading its single client through every repository operation, and returning a typed `ADDON_PASS_IN_FLIGHT` skip for same-run losers; failed unlocks will destroy rather than recycle the client.
